PLANNER='''Identify at most two unresolved observable attributes that distinguish the complete answer options. Do not request facts already explicitly supplied by the question. Choose the smallest applicable action set. Use ONLY these action kind strings: ground (localize-and-inspect), anatomy (anatomical reference), expert (focused expert observation), roi (manual original-pixel crop), paired (paired-image comparison). Natural-language descriptions and tool names are not action kind values. An action must address a stated option difference. Use actual image modality and view. A proposed diagnosis is a hypothesis, not an observation. Never apply a CXR-only tool to CT, lateral-only/montage grounding, or unconfirmed CXR. Grounding requires a frontal CXR. LLaVA-Med may describe other medical images. A classifier score cannot measure side, size, multiplicity or change. Segmentation supplies 14 anatomical regions, not lesion masks. For paired comparison identify the same object and only times explicitly stated in the question. If no available action addresses relevant uncertainty, return no actions and a reason; confidence alone is not a reason. Do not choose extra actions just to fill a budget.
For each of at most FOUR actions specify image IDs, neutral anatomical region, neutral observation question and the possible discriminating observations, without embedding the initial answer or diagnostic rationale into the question. Patient right is not display right. Any manual ROI uses stored display-pixel coordinates normalized [left,top,right,bottom], no flips. A patient-sided ROI requires a visibly read R/L marker and its normalized box; if unsure use bilateral/midline/full views. The controller converts grounding coordinates to original pixels; do not supply or reinterpret a grounding box by presumed patient side. Each ground, anatomy, roi, classifier, report, or LLaVA action binds exactly ONE current image ID. chest_xray_expert may bind one or more current CXR image IDs for one joint invocation; every selected image must be confirmed CXR. paired must bind at least TWO distinct current image IDs. Never invent image IDs. Paths are supplied by the binding layer: omit image_path and image_paths from tool_args. For segmentation, organs must be a JSON array of strings (not a string containing an array). Use only the advertised tool argument names.
Return only a small JSON object:
{"attributes":["at most two unresolved attributes"],"image_metadata":[{"image_id":"image:1","modality":"CXR|CT|other|unknown","view":"frontal|lateral|axial|montage|unknown","marker":{"text":"R|L|unknown","box":null}}],"actions":[{"kind":"ground|anatomy|expert|roi|paired","image_ids":["image:1"],"target_region":"anatomy or object","question":"neutral attribute question, no answer diagnosis","discriminating_observations":["alternative observable values"],"tool":"advertised tool for ground/anatomy/expert, otherwise empty","tool_args":{},"box":null,"target_patient_side":"unknown|right|left|bilateral|midline|not_applicable"}],"no_action_reason":"required only when no actions"}.
At most FOUR medical tool invocations and TWO new ROI/paired views. These are experimental budgets, not a paper limit. Ground automatically creates one contextual original-pixel ROI if valid boxes exist; if no box exists a provided anatomically justified broad box may be used, never interpret no box as absence. No JSON diagnostic report.'''

OBSERVER='''Inspect the original images and supplied derived views. Answer only the requested observable distinctions, citing image IDs and regions. Describe positive and relevant contrary findings in short sentences. A box or anatomical mask is a proposed location/reference, not proof of diagnosis. Separate present, absent, and not assessable. Do not infer stability from an unmeasurable difference. Tool statements are fallible hypotheses; an isolated disease name, No, or execution error is not a new patient fact. Do not choose an answer option. No initial answer or diagnostic rationale is supplied. Do not invent chronology, scale or clinical history. Return at most four short observation sentences.'''

FINAL='''Answer the original question using ALL complete options, the original images, actual derived views and the supplied observations. Expert model statements are fallible and apply only to the attributes they address. Check side, multiplicity, time point and other qualifiers when options differ on them. A coherent current-case observation may change an answer; a new unsupported disease name alone is not new evidence. Unknown is not absent, normal, stable or equal. Grounding boxes are conditional proposals, classifier scores are not option probabilities, and anatomy segmentation is not lesion segmentation or calibrated millimeters. Any legal option may be selected. Return Answer: <letter>, followed by at most three short evidence sentences. No further tools or long reasoning.'''
